    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1333">

                <pb facs="1144" n="830" xml:id="pg830"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/292</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in Russia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-10">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7:06 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>9. Russian Government is still waiting England’s action concerning Red Cross ship
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Hamburg</hi>. Papers report that ship detained at
                    request British Ambassador, Washington, as most of crew discovered to be
                    Germans. Request from beginning has caused bad impression at Foreign Office and
                    in press.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
